<title>POLAND: POLISH PEKAO BANK H1 NET RISES TO PLN 171 MLN.</title>
<headline>POLISH PEKAO BANK H1 NET RISES TO PLN 171 MLN.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary first half</p>
<p>results of the Bank Pekao SA group:</p>
<p>(in million zlotys unless stated)</p>
<p>						 H1 1997   H1 1996</p>
<p> Parent net profit			 171.30 vs 144.20</p>
<p> Parent Pre-tax profit		   276.20 vs 228.40</p>
<p> Parent profit on banking operations 590.30 vs   n.a.</p>
<p>						 June 30   Dec 31, 96</p>
<p> Parent balance sheet total	 26,735.70 vs 23,027.40</p>
<p> Parent shareholder equity	   1,258.70 vs  1,074.30</p>
<p>						  H1 1997  H1  1996</p>
<p> Group Net profit			  322.20 vs    n.a</p>
<p> Group pre-tax profit		    512.50 vs    n.a</p>
<p>						 June 30   Dec 31, 96</p>
<p>Group balance sheet total	  49,300.70 vs  42,565.70</p>
<p> Group shareholder equity	    2,413.30 vs  1,993.90</p>
<p>Note. No group results for the first half of 1996 were</p>
<p>available.</p>
<p>The Pekao Group led by Pekao Bank SA also includes Pomorski</p>
<p>Bank Kredytowy SA, Powszechny Bank Gospodarczy SA and Bank</p>
<p>Depozytowo-Kredytowy SA. The group is slated for privatisation</p>
<p>in 1998.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
